Cell["\<\
On the grids and the mesh the introduction's reading approaches the dimension \
from above, and the counting curve at its own radius from below; the two \
differ most at the small radii, which are all a finite graph has. On the \
Sierpinski graphs both readings oscillate about the Hausdorff dimension, the \
introduction's above the other at small radii.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"790ce15d-f547-4ea2-bae7-706e6556ad4c"],

Cell["\<\
The binary tree has no finite dimension under either reading: its quotients \
grow with the radius, as its ball volume grows exponentially. The two models \
settle near two as they grow.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ea4a11ef-c24e-4749-a879-489e01cffc97"],

